Classification for RPGs

In the Melvil Decimal System (MDS), the Dewey Decimal number 793.93 is used 
for “Indoor games and amusements — Other indoor diversions — Adventure games”. 
This is the most common classification for role-playing games (RPGs) in 
library catalogs.

Why 793.93?
793 = Indoor games and amusements (broad category for games played indoors) LibraryThing
793.9 = Other indoor diversions (covers activities not in the main game categories) LibraryThing
793.93 = Adventure games — a subcategory that includes RPGs, adventure games, and similar interactive storytelling games LibraryThing

This classification is widely used in U.S. public libraries and online catalogs, 
and it’s the number you’ll see for major RPG books like Player’s Handbook, 
Dungeon Master’s Guide, and Monster Manual LibraryThing.

Related subcategories
793.92 = Wargames (e.g., tabletop war games) LibraryThing
793.931 = Adventure and fantasy video games (if the RPG is video game-based)

Practical tip
If cataloging or searching for RPGs in a library, use 793.93 as the 
primary number. For video game RPGs,  might also see 793.931. This ensures 
find both tabletop and digital RPG titles in the same general location.
